  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;ERISA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ERISA refers to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act which regulates pension plans and employee benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"ERISA refers to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act, emphasizing obligations related to employee benefit plans for the Company and its subsidiaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"ERISA stands for the Employee Retirement Income Security Act of 1974, governing pension plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act, relevant in the context of financial management under the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employee Retirement Income Security Act is a federal law governing retirement plans in private industry to protect the interests of employee benefit plan participants and beneficiaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employee Retirement Income Security Act of 1974, which governs the administration of retirement plans, potentially affecting financial obligations for the Company and its affiliates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employee Retirement Income Security Act, which sets standards for pension and health plans in private industry."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df1d1358e8eeda6882c1fa2a74d036e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8390f90a484fc0fc4f7fecf58c01c94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4015d17cdefaed939b54860ada7329d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-100b5c975572f51636a61ac78458e899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21340a4ca77d2f915d79e5381c251e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13c79bc5efcb269ff90c5b5cdf07eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1348b3bb0f9a013e8a032d2005afa392</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWAP CONTRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Swap Contract is a financial agreement in which two parties exchange cash flows or liabilities from different financial instruments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A financial agreement involving various forms of swaps including interest rate swaps, which are governed by a master agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A financial contract through which two parties exchange financial instruments or cash flows."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7640e0f8a658bd7582ba0c105184de15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a35f05e33d55963235061fcfdced5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44cbda306a219cd25993684f899ea606</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERM BENCHMARK BORROWING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Borrowing defined by various standardized terms such as Term SOFR, Term CORRA, and others."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specific types of loans that follow term benchmarks for interest rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fdd35a29472aa8b0d59ccabafd832cb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c78c300be543864443a46def23942a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 'Tax' refers to a financial charge imposed by a governmental authority on individuals or organizations to fund government activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9899bf9fb2f1e9c4c871968bb39877aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUB-PARTICIPANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CLIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An entity that buys a stake in the loan rights from a Lender but is not directly involved."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0ef17404552acd85a5f0a9f77bf1ba4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CLIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A general term used to describe an individual or entity involved in the agreement or subject to its conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A generic term referring to any individual or legal entity involved in activities described in the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A legal term used to denote any individual or legal entity involved in the agreement, not limited to natural persons."&lt;SEP&gt;"A term used in the context of the agreement to refer to individuals or entities involved in the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any individual or entity referenced in the context of the Loan Document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any natural person, corporation, limited liability company, trust, joint venture, association, company, partnership, Governmental Authority or other entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"In legal and financial contexts, 'Person' refers to any individual or entity that has legal capacity to enter contracts and assume rights and obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to individuals or entities involved in agreements or contracts with lenders."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df1d1358e8eeda6882c1fa2a74d036e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7640e0f8a658bd7582ba0c105184de15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ef17404552acd85a5f0a9f77bf1ba4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5717298fa5f49a605f27b8da65de0aa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-100b5c975572f51636a61ac78458e899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21340a4ca77d2f915d79e5381c251e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4015d17cdefaed939b54860ada7329d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44cbda306a219cd25993684f899ea606</data>
    </node>
