      <data key="d2">chunk-b7295628aa9ed592731ce2c655152923</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DESIGNATED BORROWER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CLIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Applicant Borrower becomes a Designated Borrower when it meets certain conditions and receives approval from the Lenders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Designated Borrower refers to a specific entity within the Borrower's structure that may receive loans under the Agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Designated Borrower refers to any specific borrower identified in the agreement that has agreed to the loan terms and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Designated Borrower refers to specific entities that are identified to borrow under a particular loan agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Designated Borrower refers to specific parties authorized to borrow under the agreement, as designated by the Company."&lt;SEP&gt;"Designated Borrowers are subsidiaries of the Company that have specific financial obligations and loan agreements under this section."&lt;SEP&gt;"Designated borrowers are mentioned as foreign subsidiaries that have specific obligations under the loan agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Company acknowledges responsibility for obtaining information concerning the financial condition and business operations of each applicable Designated Borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"The party specifically entitled to borrow under the terms of the agreement, affecting the financial dynamics with the Administrative Agent and Lenders."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2628557ba1269917afefe40986b27b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffdbb428153c0fe1a3165c4cb2b8b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e9860cd859370389b2050b0328b04dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4112e65b1f4508cbb34a7b3f96ce6ae4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21340a4ca77d2f915d79e5381c251e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13c79bc5efcb269ff90c5b5cdf07eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fee4592c80d303ac12e768cc7a7f8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dfde67bcc6c4100358b49b218bb541&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a35f05e33d55963235061fcfdced5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATERIAL ADVERSE EFFECT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A legal term that refers to significant negative changes or constraints that could impact a company's financial condition or operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A significant negative impact on the financial condition or operations of a Borrower or its Subsidiaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Material Adverse Effect describes situations that significantly change or impact a company's financial condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Material Adverse Effect indicates significant negative impacts that might affect the financial condition or operations of the Company."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f13c79bc5efcb269ff90c5b5cdf07eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a35f05e33d55963235061fcfdced5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a32da08942b4e8f9bb0977d0f91b0056&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80e94d1815c3927a9d45e840b95ae93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOAN AGREEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Loan Agreement refers to the specific contract outlining the terms and conditions between the Company and the Lenders regarding the loans issued."&lt;SEP&gt;"The formalization of the terms and conditions under which the loan is made, including repayment and interest."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1348b3bb0f9a013e8a032d2005afa392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5717298fa5f49a605f27b8da65de0aa3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEES AND CHARGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fees and Charges refer to the additional costs associated with the borrowing and services rendered throughout the term of the loans."</data>
