      <data key="d1">"Base Rate means the highest of NYFRB Rate, Prime Rate, and Term SOFR for determining interest rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Base Rate refers to the minimum interest rate set by a central bank (in this case, the applicable financial agreement), below which banks are not expected to lend."&lt;SEP&gt;"Default Rate means an interest rate equal to the Base Rate plus the Applicable Rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minimum interest rate set by banks for loans."</data>
