    <node id="&quot;INTEREST PERIOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An Interest Period typically lasts one month and is applied to Term Benchmark Loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Period is the duration for which interest is calculated on a loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Period refers to the length of time over which interest is calculated for specific loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Period refers to the specified timeframe for which interest rates are calculated under the agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specified duration during which a borrowing rate is applicable."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Interest Period defines the time frame for which interest rates on loans apply, relevant for the adjustment of benchmark rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The duration for which the interest rate on a loan is fixed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The duration over which interest is calculated for the loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The specific duration for which interest rates are calculated for a loan, often aligned with payment schedules."</data>
