      <data key="d1">"Base Rate Loans are loans that use the Base Rate as a benchmark for interest calculations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Base Rate Loans are loans with interest rates that are determined by a set base rate pricing structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loans denominated in US Dollars that can be borrowed, converted, or continued as Base Rate Loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loans that are tied to a base interest rate, typically lower than other types of loans and used for various borrowing purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loans that are tied to a specific base interest rate set by the lending institution."</data>
