    <node id="&quot;TERM SOFR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A secured overnight financing rate that reflects the cost of borrowing cash overnight collateralized by U.S. Treasuries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Secured Overnight Financing Rate used as a benchmark for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Term SOFR (Secured Overnight Financing Rate) is a benchmark interest rate for dollar loans and reflects the cost of borrowing cash, secured by U.S. Treasury securities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Term SOFR Reference Rate for borrowing in US Dollars, determined at specific intervals prior to the commencement of a loan period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Term SOFR is a benchmark interest rate used for loans as part of the agreement, indicating the cost of borrowing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fdd35a29472aa8b0d59ccabafd832cb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c78c300be543864443a46def23942a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7398756e5d9f35912e2cc6d9774a28be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e9860cd859370389b2050b0328b04dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-100b5c975572f51636a61ac78458e899</data>
    </node>
