    <node id="&quot;BENCHMARK TRANSITION EVENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A 'Benchmark Transition Event' signifies a situation where a widely-used benchmark interest rate is replaced or adjusted due to market changes or regulatory requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Benchmark Transition Event indicates significant changes in benchmark settings, prompting the necessity for adjustments in loan agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Benchmark Transition Event occurs when the current benchmark for loans is no longer provided or representative, triggering a replacement process."&lt;SEP&gt;"An event that leads to the determination of an alternative rate of interest following the discontinuation of the existing interest rate benchmark."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2eab36c3a28bbe2353185d3b7d97705d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9899bf9fb2f1e9c4c871968bb39877aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5717298fa5f49a605f27b8da65de0aa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7398756e5d9f35912e2cc6d9774a28be</data>
    </node>
